#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/currency.html.j2:10
msgid ""
"Maintenance costs are stored as plain numbers. This setting says which "
"currency those numbers are in and how they are formatted."
msgstr ""
"Onderhoudskosten worden opgeslagen als kale getallen. Deze instelling "
"bepaalt in welke valuta die getallen staan en hoe ze worden opgemaakt."

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/currency.html.j2:14
msgid "Currency code"
msgstr "Valutacode"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/currency.html.j2:18
msgid ""
"ISO 4217 code, for instance EUR, USD, CHF, or GBP. Leave empty to show "
"bare numbers without a currency."
msgstr ""
"ISO 4217-code, bijvoorbeeld EUR, USD, CHF of GBP. Laat leeg om kale "
"getallen zonder valuta te tonen."

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/currency.html.j2:26
#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/tile-rendering.html.j2:24
msgid "Preview"
msgstr "Voorbeeld"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/currency.html.j2:31
#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/language.html.j2:32
msgid "Note"
msgstr "Opmerking"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/currency.html.j2:32
msgid ""
"There is a single currency for all entries and no conversion. Changing "
"the code relabels existing amounts, it does not convert them. If you buy "
"equipment abroad, convert the amount yourself before entering it."
msgstr ""
"Er is één valuta voor alle vermeldingen en geen omrekening. Een "
"gewijzigde code geeft bestaande bedragen alleen een ander label, hij "
"rekent ze niet om. Als je uitrusting in het buitenland koopt, reken het "
"bedrag dan zelf om vóór het invoeren."

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/duplicate-matching.html.j2:10
msgid ""
"If you import the same activity from two different sources (e.g. a device"
" import and a later Strava archive), they will not be recognized as "
"duplicates by content hash, since the files differ. This looks for "
"activities from different sources with a similar start time, distance, "
"and duration instead, and lists them under Settings → Possible Duplicates"
" for you to merge."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/duplicate-matching.html.j2:15
msgid "Detect cross-source duplicate candidates"
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/duplicate-matching.html.j2:19
msgid "Start time tolerance / s"
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/duplicate-matching.html.j2:21
msgid ""
"Two activities from different sources are only considered candidates if "
"their start times are within this many seconds of each other."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/duplicate-matching.html.j2:25
#, python-format
msgid "Distance/duration tolerance / %%"
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/duplicate-matching.html.j2:27
msgid ""
"Where both activities have a distance or elapsed time, they must agree "
"within this percentage."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/duplicate-matching.html.j2:32
msgid "Automatically merge candidates using the priority order below"
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/duplicate-matching.html.j2:35
msgid "Source priority"
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/duplicate-matching.html.j2:36
msgid ""
"When automatic merging is on and a candidate pair is found, the activity "
"from the lower-numbered source is kept and the other is removed (its "
"source file stays untouched and is excluded from future re-import). Equal"
" numbers are never auto-resolved and are left for manual review instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/excluded-activities.html.j2:10
msgid ""
"These activities are not imported: either the file could not be read, or "
"you deleted the activity. They are remembered so that they are not "
"retried and re-logged on every import scan. Source data is never deleted,"
" so re-importing an activity here brings it back on the next import scan."
msgstr ""
"Deze activiteiten worden niet geïmporteerd: het bestand kon niet worden "
"gelezen, of je hebt de activiteit verwijderd. Ze worden onthouden zodat "
"ze niet bij elke importscan opnieuw worden geprobeerd en gelogd. "
"Brongegevens worden nooit verwijderd, dus een activiteit hier opnieuw "
"importeren brengt haar bij de volgende importscan terug."

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/excluded-activities.html.j2:13
msgid "Are you sure you want to retry all failed imports on the next import scan?"
msgstr ""
"Weet je zeker dat je alle mislukte importen bij de volgende importscan "
"opnieuw wilt proberen?"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/excluded-activities.html.j2:14
msgid "Retry all failed imports"
msgstr "Alle mislukte importen opnieuw proberen"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/excluded-activities.html.j2:21
msgid "Source"
msgstr "Bron"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/excluded-activities.html.j2:23
msgid "Reason"
msgstr "Reden"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/excluded-activities.html.j2:24
msgid "Details"
msgstr "Details"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/excluded-activities.html.j2:25
msgid "Last attempt"
msgstr "Laatste poging"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/excluded-activities.html.j2:48
msgid "No excluded activities recorded."
msgstr "Geen uitgesloten activiteiten geregistreerd."

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-counted-activities.html.j2:10
msgid ""
"Only the selected kinds count toward explorer tiles, clusters and "
"squares. Leave everything unselected to count every activity. This is "
"where you exclude the kinds you were not moving under your own power, "
"such as car or train rides."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-counted-activities.html.j2:12
msgid ""
"A kind that you add later is not selected automatically, so its "
"activities will not count until you come back here and select it."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-counted-activities.html.j2:25
msgid ""
"Changing this rebuilds the tile visits from the stored activity tiles. "
"Nothing is re-imported, but it takes a moment."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-tiles.html.j2:10
msgid ""
"Tiles that you have marked as inaccessible cannot be reached, so they "
"will stay missing forever and can block a cluster or a square from "
"growing. You can let them count as covered for the purpose of cluster and"
" square geometry."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-tiles.html.j2:12
msgid ""
"They never count as visited tiles: your explored tile counts stay honest,"
" and the map keeps drawing them in the inaccessible style. Counting is "
"off by default, which is the stricter game."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-tiles.html.j2:14
msgid ""
"Inaccessible tiles are counted from the origin of time, as if they had "
"always been covered. Enabling this therefore also changes the past in the"
" cluster and square evolution plots."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-tiles.html.j2:21
msgid "Count inaccessible tiles toward cluster and square"
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-tiles.html.j2:27
msgid ""
"Tiles are marked as inaccessible per zoom level, so marking a tile on the"
" zoom 14 map does not mark the corresponding zoom 17 tiles."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-zoom-levels.html.j2:4
#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-zoom-levels.html.j2:8
msgid "Explorer Zoom Levels"
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-zoom-levels.html.j2:10
msgid ""
"Choose the zoom levels for which explorer tiles, clusters, and squares "
"are computed. Each enabled level gets its own page in the Explorer menu, "
"its own map overlays, and its own square planner."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-zoom-levels.html.j2:12
msgid ""
"Zoom 14 are the classic explorer tiles, zoom 17 are the squadratinhos. "
"Every additional level costs computation time on import and storage in "
"the database; disabling a level discards its cluster and square history, "
"but the recorded tile visits stay, so it can be enabled again later."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-zoom-levels.html.j2:14
msgid ""
"Each zoom level splits every tile into four, so the number of tiles "
"quadruples per level. Zoom 18 is therefore about 4 times and zoom 19 "
"about 16 times as compute and storage intense as zoom 17."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/explorer-zoom-levels.html.j2:22
#, python-format
msgid "%(factor)d times as compute intense as zoom 17."
msgstr ""

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/hammerhead.html.j2:8
msgid "Hammerhead Connect"
msgstr "Hammerhead verbinden"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/hammerhead.html.j2:12
msgid ""
"You can connect to the Hammerhead Karoo API so that rides recorded on "
"your Karoo head unit are downloaded automatically."
msgstr ""
"Je kunt verbinding maken met de Hammerhead Karoo API zodat ritten die op "
"je Karoo zijn opgenomen automatisch worden gedownload."

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/hammerhead.html.j2:14
msgid ""
"Hammerhead does not offer a shared OAuth application, so you need to "
"register your own developer account:"
msgstr ""
"Hammerhead biedt geen gedeelde OAuth-applicatie, dus je moet een eigen "
"ontwikkelaarsaccount registreren:"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/hammerhead.html.j2:16
msgid "Create a developer account at"
msgstr "Maak een ontwikkelaarsaccount aan op"

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/hammerhead.html.j2:17
msgid ""
"Enable developer settings for your account, fill in the app name and "
"description, and accept the API Licensing agreement."
msgstr ""
"Schakel de ontwikkelaarsinstellingen voor je account in, vul de app-naam "
"en beschrijving in en accepteer de API-licentieovereenkomst."

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/hammerhead.html.j2:18
msgid ""
"Open the API settings tab that appears after accepting the agreement — "
"your client ID and client secret are listed there."
msgstr ""
"Open het tabblad met API-instellingen dat na het accepteren van de "
"overeenkomst verschijnt — daar staan je client-ID en client secret."

#: src/geo_activity_playground/webui/templates/settings/hammerhead.html.j2:21
msgid ""
